    "body": "Infinity in model analysis is clamped to confidence 1.0, allowing malformed confidence values to satisfy the automatic assignment threshold. Treat non-finite confidence as the default before clamping.\n\nValidation: non-finite numeric and string forms fail the baseline regression and pass with the fix; valid confidence remains unchanged. CPU unit tests use the actual helper and no external mutations. Test formatting, source import sorting, and Python compilation pass.\n\nReview requested: @NVIDIA/mcore-oncall. This PR is ready for review with CPU regression evidence above. Upstream runner validation remains subject to NVIDIA contributor vetting.\n",
    "changed_files": 2,
